{
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# Spotify Top 50 Playlist Songs - Academic Analysis\n",
                "\n",
                "**Data Visualization Project**  \n",
                "**Dataset**: [Spotify Top 50 Playlist Songs by Anxods](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anxods/spotify-top-50-playlist-songs-anxods)  \n",
                "**Date**: January 2026\n",
                "\n",
                "---"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 1. Project Overview\n",
                "\n",
                "### Goal\n",
                "This analysis aims to explore global music consumption patterns by examining Spotify's Top 50 charts across multiple countries. We investigate:\n",
                "- How explicit content varies across different cultural regions\n",
                "- The globalization of music: which artists and tracks transcend borders\n",
                "- Regional differences in music preferences\n",
                "- Temporal trends in track characteristics\n",
                "\n",
                "### Dataset Description\n",
                "The dataset contains daily snapshots of Spotify's Top 50 charts from various countries including:\n",
                "- **Western countries**: USA, UK, France, Spain, Italy, Argentina, Mexico\n",
                "- **Asian countries**: Japan, South Korea\n",
                "- **Global chart**: World\n",
                "\n",
                "Each record includes:\n",
                "- Track information (name, artist, duration)\n",
                "- Chart position and date\n",
                "- Explicit content flag\n",
                "- Streaming statistics\n",
                "\n",
                "---"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2. Environment Setup"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Data manipulation\n",
                "import pandas as pd\n",
                "import numpy as np\n",
                "import glob\n",
                "import os\n",
                "from datetime import datetime\n",
                "\n",
                "# Data visualization\n",
                "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                "import seaborn as sns\n",
                "import plotly.express as px\n",
                "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
                "from plotly.subplots import make_subplots\n",
                "\n",
                "# Statistical analysis\n",
                "from scipy import stats\n",
                "\n",
                "# Suppress warnings for cleaner output\n",
                "import warnings\n",
                "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
                "\n",
                "# Display settings\n",
                "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\n",
                "pd.set_option('display.max_rows', 100)\n",
                "pd.set_option('display.float_format', '{:.2f}'.format)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Visualization style\n",
                "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-darkgrid')\n",
                "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Plotly template\n",
                "import plotly.io as pio\n",
                "pio.templates.default = \"plotly_dark\"\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"✓ All libraries imported successfully\")\n",
                "print(f\"Python version: {pd.__version__} (pandas)\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3. Data Loading\n",
                "\n",
                "We load all CSV files from the Kaggle dataset. Each file represents a different country's Top 50 chart."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Define data directory (adjust path as needed)\n",
                "DATA_DIR = r\"c:\\Users\\bebab\\Desktop\\Università\\Data Visualization\\DataVisProjectSpotify\"\n",
                "\n",
                "# Country mapping for cleaner names\n",
                "COUNTRY_MAP = {\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-argentina': 'Argentina',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-france': 'France',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-italy': 'Italy',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-japan': 'Japan',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-mexico': 'Mexico',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-south-korea': 'South Korea',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-spain': 'Spain',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-uk': 'UK',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-usa': 'USA',\n",
                "    'spotify-streaming-top-50-world': 'World'\n",
                "}\n",
                "\n",
                "# Load all CSV files\n",
                "csv_files = glob.glob(os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"spotify-streaming-top-50-*.csv\"))\n",
                "print(f\"Found {len(csv_files)} CSV files\\n\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Display basic information for each file\n",
                "for file_path in sorted(csv_files):\n",
                "    filename = os.path.basename(file_path).replace('.csv', '')\n",
                "    country = COUNTRY_MAP.get(filename, filename)\n",
                "    df_temp = pd.read_csv(file_path)\n",
                "    print(f\"{country:15s} | {df_temp.shape[0]:6,} rows | {df_temp.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"\\n✓ Files loaded successfully\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Load and preview a single file to understand structure\n",
                "sample_file = csv_files[0]\n",
                "df_sample = pd.read_csv(sample_file)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Sample Data Structure:\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nShape: {df_sample.shape}\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nColumns: {list(df_sample.columns)}\")\n",
                "print(\"\\nFirst 5 rows:\")\n",
                "df_sample.head()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Display data types and missing values\n",
                "print(\"Data Types and Missing Values:\")\n",
                "df_sample.info()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 4. Data Understanding\n",
                "\n",
                "### Key Variables\n",
                "\n",
                "Based on the sample data, we identify the following key variables:\n",
                "\n",
                "- **date**: Date when the track was in the chart (temporal dimension)\n",
                "- **position**: Rank in the Top 50 (1 = #1 hit)\n",
                "- **song**: Track name\n",
                "- **artist**: Artist or band name\n",
                "- **streams**: Number of streams on that date\n",
                "- **duration_ms**: Track length in milliseconds\n",
                "- **is_explicit**: Boolean flag for explicit content\n",
                "- **country**: (to be added during integration)\n",
                "\n",
                "### Potential Data Issues\n",
                "\n",
                "We need to check for:\n",
                "1. **Missing values**: Particularly in artist names or song titles\n",
                "2. **Data type inconsistencies**: Date formats, boolean values as strings\n",
                "3. **Duplicate records**: Same song/date/country combinations\n",
                "4. **Outliers**: Unrealistic stream counts or durations\n",
                "5. **Inconsistent naming**: Artist/song name variations across countries"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Check for missing values in sample\n",
                "print(\"Missing Values Analysis:\")\n",
                "print(df_sample.isnull().sum())\n",
                "print(f\"\\nTotal missing values: {df_sample.isnull().sum().sum()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Percentage: {(df_sample.isnull().sum().sum() / df_sample.size) * 100:.2f}%\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Check unique values for categorical variables\n",
                "print(\"Unique Value Counts:\")\n",
                "print(f\"Unique songs: {df_sample['song'].nunique()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Unique artists: {df_sample['artist'].nunique()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Explicit content values: {df_sample['is_explicit'].unique()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nDate range: {df_sample['date'].min()} to {df_sample['date'].max()}\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 5. Data Cleaning\n",
                "\n",
                "We perform systematic data cleaning to ensure consistency and quality."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "def clean_dataframe(df, country_name):\n",
                "    \"\"\"\n",
                "    Clean a single country's dataframe.\n",
                "    \n",
                "    Steps:\n",
                "    1. Standardize column names (lowercase, underscores)\n",
                "    2. Convert date to datetime\n",
                "    3. Convert is_explicit to boolean\n",
                "    4. Handle missing values\n",
                "    5. Remove duplicates\n",
                "    6. Add country column\n",
                "    \"\"\"\n",
                "    # Make a copy to avoid modifying original\n",
                "    df = df.copy()\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 1: Standardize column names\n",
                "    df.columns = df.columns.str.lower().str.replace(' ', '_')\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 2: Convert date to datetime\n",
                "    df['date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['date'], errors='coerce')\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 3: Convert is_explicit to boolean\n",
                "    # Handle both string ('True'/'False') and boolean values\n",
                "    if df['is_explicit'].dtype == 'object':\n",
                "        df['is_explicit'] = df['is_explicit'].map({\n",
                "            'True': True, 'true': True, 'TRUE': True, True: True,\n",
                "            'False': False, 'false': False, 'FALSE': False, False: False\n",
                "        })\n",
                "    df['is_explicit'] = df['is_explicit'].astype(bool)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 4: Handle missing values\n",
                "    # Drop rows with missing critical information\n",
                "    before_drop = len(df)\n",
                "    df = df.dropna(subset=['date', 'song', 'artist'])\n",
                "    after_drop = len(df)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    if before_drop != after_drop:\n",
                "        print(f\"  {country_name}: Dropped {before_drop - after_drop} rows with missing critical data\")\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Fill missing numeric values with median\n",
                "    numeric_cols = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number]).columns\n",
                "    for col in numeric_cols:\n",
                "        if df[col].isnull().any():\n",
                "            df[col].fillna(df[col].median(), inplace=True)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 5: Remove duplicates\n",
                "    # Consider duplicates: same song, artist, date, and country\n",
                "    before_dedup = len(df)\n",
                "    df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=['date', 'song', 'artist', 'position'], keep='first')\n",
                "    after_dedup = len(df)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    if before_dedup != after_dedup:\n",
                "        print(f\"  {country_name}: Removed {before_dedup - after_dedup} duplicate rows\")\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 6: Add country column\n",
                "    df['country'] = country_name\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Step 7: Convert duration_ms to minutes for easier interpretation\n",
                "    if 'duration_ms' in df.columns:\n",
                "        df['duration_min'] = df['duration_ms'] / 60000\n",
                "    \n",
                "    return df\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Cleaning individual country datasets...\\n\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Clean each file\n",
                "cleaned_dfs = []\n",
                "for file_path in sorted(csv_files):\n",
                "    filename = os.path.basename(file_path).replace('.csv', '')\n",
                "    country = COUNTRY_MAP.get(filename, filename)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    df_raw = pd.read_csv(file_path)\n",
                "    df_clean = clean_dataframe(df_raw, country)\n",
                "    cleaned_dfs.append(df_clean)\n",
                "    \n",
                "print(\"\\n✓ All datasets cleaned successfully\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 6. Data Integration\n",
                "\n",
                "We merge all country-specific datasets into a single unified dataframe for comprehensive analysis."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Concatenate all cleaned dataframes\n",
                "df_combined = pd.concat(cleaned_dfs, ignore_index=True)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Reorder columns to put country first\n",
                "cols = ['country'] + [col for col in df_combined.columns if col != 'country']\n",
                "df_combined = df_combined[cols]\n",
                "\n",
                "# Reset index\n",
                "df_combined.reset_index(drop=True, inplace=True)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Unified Dataset Summary:\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nTotal records: {len(df_combined):,}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Countries: {df_combined['country'].nunique()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Unique songs: {df_combined['song'].nunique():,}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Unique artists: {df_combined['artist'].nunique():,}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Date range: {df_combined['date'].min().date()} to {df_combined['date'].max().date()}\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nMemory usage: {df_combined.memory_usage(deep=True).sum() / 1024**2:.2f} MB\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Validate the merged dataset\n",
                "print(\"Validation Checks:\\n\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Check 1: Distribution across countries\n",
                "print(\"Records per country:\")\n",
                "print(df_combined['country'].value_counts().sort_index())\n",
                "\n",
                "# Check 2: Missing values\n",
                "print(f\"\\nMissing values: {df_combined.isnull().sum().sum()}\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Check 3: Data types\n",
                "print(\"\\nData types:\")\n",
                "print(df_combined.dtypes)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Display first few rows of unified dataset\n",
                "print(\"First 10 rows of unified dataset:\")\n",
                "df_combined.head(10)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 7. Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
                "\n",
                "We perform descriptive statistical analysis to understand the data distribution and key patterns."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Descriptive statistics for numeric variables\n",
                "print(\"Descriptive Statistics:\")\n",
                "df_combined.describe()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 7.1 Distribution of Explicit Content"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Overall explicit content percentage\n",
                "explicit_count = df_combined['is_explicit'].sum()\n",
                "explicit_pct = (explicit_count / len(df_combined)) * 100\n",
                "\n",
                "print(f\"Global Explicit Content:\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Explicit tracks: {explicit_count:,} ({explicit_pct:.2f}%)\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Non-explicit: {len(df_combined) - explicit_count:,} ({100 - explicit_pct:.2f}%)\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Explicit content by country\n",
                "print(\"\\nExplicit Content by Country:\")\n",
                "explicit_by_country = df_combined.groupby('country')['is_explicit'].agg([\n",
                "    ('total_tracks', 'count'),\n",
                "    ('explicit_tracks', 'sum'),\n",
                "    ('explicit_pct', lambda x: (x.sum() / len(x)) * 100)\n",
                "]).sort_values('explicit_pct', ascending=False)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(explicit_by_country)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Visualize explicit content distribution\n",
                "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
                "\n",
                "# Pie chart for overall distribution\n",
                "explicit_data = df_combined['is_explicit'].value_counts()\n",
                "axes[0].pie(explicit_data, labels=['Non-Explicit', 'Explicit'], autopct='%1.1f%%',\n",
                "            colors=['#1DB954', '#FF6B6B'], startangle=90)\n",
                "axes[0].set_title('Overall Explicit Content Distribution', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "\n",
                "# Bar chart by country\n",
                "explicit_by_country['explicit_pct'].plot(kind='barh', ax=axes[1], color='#FF6B6B')\n",
                "axes[1].set_xlabel('Explicit Content (%)', fontsize=12)\n",
                "axes[1].set_title('Explicit Content by Country', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "axes[1].grid(axis='x', alpha=0.3)\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 7.2 Song Duration Analysis"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Duration statistics\n",
                "print(\"Song Duration Statistics (in minutes):\")\n",
                "print(f\"\\nMean: {df_combined['duration_min'].mean():.2f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Median: {df_combined['duration_min'].median():.2f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Std Dev: {df_combined['duration_min'].std():.2f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Min: {df_combined['duration_min'].min():.2f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Max: {df_combined['duration_min'].max():.2f}\")\n",
                "\n",
                "# Duration by country\n",
                "print(\"\\nAverage Duration by Country:\")\n",
                "duration_by_country = df_combined.groupby('country')['duration_min'].mean().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
                "print(duration_by_country)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Visualize duration distribution\n",
                "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
                "\n",
                "# Histogram\n",
                "axes[0].hist(df_combined['duration_min'], bins=50, color='#1DB954', edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7)\n",
                "axes[0].axvline(df_combined['duration_min'].mean(), color='red', linestyle='--', \n",
                "                linewidth=2, label=f'Mean: {df_combined[\"duration_min\"].mean():.2f} min')\n",
                "axes[0].axvline(df_combined['duration_min'].median(), color='orange', linestyle='--', \n",
                "                linewidth=2, label=f'Median: {df_combined[\"duration_min\"].median():.2f} min')\n",
                "axes[0].set_xlabel('Duration (minutes)', fontsize=12)\n",
                "axes[0].set_ylabel('Frequency', fontsize=12)\n",
                "axes[0].set_title('Distribution of Song Duration', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "axes[0].legend()\n",
                "axes[0].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Box plot by country\n",
                "df_combined.boxplot(column='duration_min', by='country', ax=axes[1], patch_artist=True)\n",
                "axes[1].set_xlabel('Country', fontsize=12)\n",
                "axes[1].set_ylabel('Duration (minutes)', fontsize=12)\n",
                "axes[1].set_title('Song Duration by Country', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "axes[1].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=45)\n",
                "plt.suptitle('')  # Remove default title\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 7.3 Rank Distribution Analysis"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Analyze top positions\n",
                "print(\"Most Frequent Songs in Top 10:\")\n",
                "top10 = df_combined[df_combined['position'] <= 10]\n",
                "top10_songs = top10.groupby(['song', 'artist']).size().sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)\n",
                "print(top10_songs)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Number of times each position appears\n",
                "position_counts = df_combined['position'].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
                "print(f\"\\nTotal entries per position (should be similar):\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Mean: {position_counts.mean():.0f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Std: {position_counts.std():.0f}\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 7.4 Temporal Analysis"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Add temporal features\n",
                "df_combined['year'] = df_combined['date'].dt.year\n",
                "df_combined['month'] = df_combined['date'].dt.month\n",
                "df_combined['day_of_week'] = df_combined['date'].dt.day_name()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Entries by month\n",
                "print(\"Data Entries by Month:\")\n",
                "monthly_counts = df_combined.groupby(df_combined['date'].dt.to_period('M')).size()\n",
                "print(monthly_counts)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Plot temporal distribution\n",
                "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
                "monthly_counts.plot(ax=ax, marker='o', color='#1DB954', linewidth=2)\n",
                "ax.set_xlabel('Month', fontsize=12)\n",
                "ax.set_ylabel('Number of Entries', fontsize=12)\n",
                "ax.set_title('Data Coverage Over Time', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
                "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 8. Comparative Analysis\n",
                "\n",
                "We compare music patterns across cultural regions and identify global vs. local trends."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 8.1 Regional Classification"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Define regional groupings\n",
                "REGIONS = {\n",
                "    'Western Europe': ['France', 'Italy', 'Spain', 'UK'],\n",
                "    'Americas': ['USA', 'Argentina', 'Mexico'],\n",
                "    'Asia': ['Japan', 'South Korea'],\n",
                "    'Global': ['World']\n",
                "}\n",
                "\n",
                "# Create reverse mapping\n",
                "country_to_region = {}\n",
                "for region, countries in REGIONS.items():\n",
                "    for country in countries:\n",
                "        country_to_region[country] = region\n",
                "\n",
                "# Add region column\n",
                "df_combined['region'] = df_combined['country'].map(country_to_region)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Regional Distribution:\")\n",
                "print(df_combined['region'].value_counts())"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 8.2 Western vs Asian Markets Comparison"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Exclude 'World' for regional comparison\n",
                "df_regional = df_combined[df_combined['region'] != 'Global'].copy()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Compare explicit content\n",
                "print(\"Explicit Content by Region:\")\n",
                "regional_explicit = df_regional.groupby('region')['is_explicit'].agg([\n",
                "    ('total', 'count'),\n",
                "    ('explicit', 'sum'),\n",
                "    ('pct', lambda x: (x.sum() / len(x)) * 100)\n",
                "])\n",
                "print(regional_explicit)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Compare duration\n",
                "print(\"\\nAverage Duration by Region:\")\n",
                "regional_duration = df_regional.groupby('region')['duration_min'].agg(['mean', 'median', 'std'])\n",
                "print(regional_duration)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Statistical test: Is explicit content significantly different between Asia and Western regions?\n",
                "asia_explicit = df_regional[df_regional['region'] == 'Asia']['is_explicit']\n",
                "western_europe_explicit = df_regional[df_regional['region'] == 'Western Europe']['is_explicit']\n",
                "americas_explicit = df_regional[df_regional['region'] == 'Americas']['is_explicit']\n",
                "\n",
                "# Chi-square test\n",
                "from scipy.stats import chi2_contingency\n",
                "\n",
                "# Create contingency table\n",
                "contingency_table = pd.crosstab(df_regional['region'], df_regional['is_explicit'])\n",
                "chi2, p_value, dof, expected = chi2_contingency(contingency_table)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"\\nChi-Square Test for Explicit Content Across Regions:\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Chi-square statistic: {chi2:.4f}\")\n",
                "print(f\"  P-value: {p_value:.4e}\")\n",
                "print(f\"  Degrees of freedom: {dof}\")\n",
                "\n",
                "if p_value < 0.05:\n",
                "    print(\"  ✓ Significant difference found (p < 0.05)\")\n",
                "else:\n",
                "    print(\"  ✗ No significant difference (p >= 0.05)\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 8.3 Global vs Local Music Patterns"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Identify truly global songs (appearing in multiple countries)\n",
                "song_country_count = df_combined.groupby(['song', 'artist'])['country'].nunique().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Top 20 Most Global Songs (appearing in most countries):\")\n",
                "print(song_country_count.head(20))\n",
                "\n",
                "# Calculate globality score\n",
                "max_countries = df_combined['country'].nunique()\n",
                "globality_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
                "    'song_artist': song_country_count.index.map(lambda x: f\"{x[0]} - {x[1]}\"),\n",
                "    'countries': song_country_count.values,\n",
                "    'globality_score': (song_country_count.values / max_countries) * 100\n",
                "}).head(20)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(f\"\\nGlobality Score (out of {max_countries} countries):\")\n",
                "print(globality_df)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Identify most global artists\n",
                "artist_country_count = df_combined.groupby('artist')['country'].nunique().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Top 20 Most Global Artists:\")\n",
                "top_global_artists = artist_country_count.head(20)\n",
                "print(top_global_artists)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Total appearances\n",
                "artist_appearances = df_combined.groupby('artist').size().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Combine metrics\n",
                "artist_metrics = pd.DataFrame({\n",
                "    'countries': artist_country_count,\n",
                "    'total_appearances': artist_appearances\n",
                "}).sort_values('countries', ascending=False).head(20)\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"\\nTop Global Artists (countries + appearances):\")\n",
                "print(artist_metrics)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 8.4 Cultural Differences in Music Preferences"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Compare average chart position of explicit vs non-explicit content\n",
                "print(\"Average Chart Position by Explicit Content:\")\n",
                "position_by_explicit = df_combined.groupby(['region', 'is_explicit'])['position'].mean().unstack()\n",
                "print(position_by_explicit)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Song diversity: unique songs per country\n",
                "print(\"\\nSong Diversity by Country:\")\n",
                "diversity = df_combined.groupby('country').agg({\n",
                "    'song': 'nunique',\n",
                "    'artist': 'nunique'\n",
                "}).rename(columns={'song': 'unique_songs', 'artist': 'unique_artists'})\n",
                "print(diversity.sort_values('unique_songs', ascending=False))"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 9. Data Visualization\n",
                "\n",
                "We create comprehensive visualizations to communicate our findings effectively."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 9.1 Explicit Content Heatmap by Chart Position"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Create matrix: position (rows) x country (columns), values = % explicit\n",
                "heatmap_data = pd.DataFrame(index=range(1, 51), columns=sorted(df_combined['country'].unique()))\n",
                "\n",
                "for country in heatmap_data.columns:\n",
                "    country_data = df_combined[df_combined['country'] == country]\n",
                "    for pos in range(1, 51):\n",
                "        pos_data = country_data[country_data['position'] == pos]\n",
                "        if len(pos_data) > 0:\n",
                "            explicit_pct = (pos_data['is_explicit'].sum() / len(pos_data)) * 100\n",
                "            heatmap_data.loc[pos, country] = explicit_pct\n",
                "        else:\n",
                "            heatmap_data.loc[pos, country] = 0\n",
                "\n",
                "heatmap_data = heatmap_data.astype(float)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Plot heatmap\n",
                "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 14))\n",
                "\n",
                "sns.heatmap(heatmap_data, cmap='YlOrRd', cbar_kws={'label': '% Explicit Content'},\n",
                "            linewidths=0.5, linecolor='gray', ax=ax, vmin=0, vmax=100)\n",
                "\n",
                "ax.set_xlabel('Country', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "ax.set_ylabel('Chart Position', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "ax.set_title('Explicit Content Distribution Across Chart Positions and Countries',\n",
                "             fontsize=15, fontweight='bold', pad=20)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Set y-axis to show every 5th position\n",
                "yticks = [0, 4, 9, 14, 19, 24, 29, 34, 39, 44, 49]\n",
                "yticklabels = [1, 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40, 45, 50]\n",
                "ax.set_yticks(yticks)\n",
                "ax.set_yticklabels(yticklabels, rotation=0)\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Heatmap shows where explicit content tends to appear in the Top 50 charts.\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 9.2 Regional Comparison Bar Charts"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Create comparative visualizations\n",
                "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(16, 12))\n",
                "\n",
                "# 1. Explicit content by country\n",
                "explicit_by_country['explicit_pct'].sort_values().plot(\n",
                "    kind='barh', ax=axes[0, 0], color='#FF6B6B'\n",
                ")\n",
                "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel('Explicit Content (%)', fontsize=11)\n",
                "axes[0, 0].set_title('Explicit Content Percentage by Country', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
                "axes[0, 0].grid(axis='x', alpha=0.3)\n",
