            "source": [
                "## 10. Key Insights\n",
                "\n",
                "Based on our comprehensive analysis, we summarize the most important findings:"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Finding 1: Significant Regional Differences in Explicit Content\n",
                "\n",
                "**Observation**: Explicit content varies dramatically across cultural regions:\n",
                "- Americas show the highest percentage of explicit content\n",
                "- Asian markets (Japan, South Korea) have significantly lower explicit content\n",
                "- Western European countries fall in the middle\n",
                "\n",
                "**Statistical Significance**: Chi-square test confirms these differences are statistically significant (p < 0.05)\n",
                "\n",
                "**Interpretation**: Cultural norms and content regulations strongly influence what music becomes popular in different regions."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Finding 2: Limited True Globalization\n",
                "\n",
                "**Observation**: \n",
                "- Very few songs appear in all countries simultaneously\n",
                "- Most \"global hits\" are concentrated in culturally similar regions\n",
                "- Asian markets show distinct preferences from Western markets\n",
                "\n",
                "**Interpretation**: Despite streaming platforms enabling global access, local cultural preferences remain strong. Music consumption is still heavily influenced by language, culture, and regional tastes."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Finding 3: Duration Patterns Vary by Region\n",
                "\n",
                "**Observation**:\n",
                "- Average song duration is relatively consistent globally (3-3.5 minutes)\n",
                "- Some regional variations exist but are modest\n",
                "- Temporal trends show slight decrease in duration over time\n",
                "\n",
                "**Interpretation**: Song duration appears to be more universally standardized than content type, possibly due to platform algorithms and attention span considerations."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### Finding 4: Explicit Content Not Concentrated at Bottom of Charts\n",
                "\n",
                "**Observation**: The heatmap reveals that explicit content is distributed throughout chart positions, not just relegated to lower ranks.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Interpretation**: In markets where explicit content is accepted, it performs well commercially and reaches top chart positions."
            ]
        },
